  "hypotheses": [
    "The proposed4um-wide shunt length5to7.4um change reduces nominal pull-down conductance. Its intended higher LP/LN common mode might lift upper-master emitters and selector collectors, improving minimum selector VCE. This direction is not a measured benefit.",
    "The same LP/LN nodes are the collectors of cold-failing gain HBTs59/60/111/112. Holding their emitter voltage fixed, raising LP/LN increases signed VCE. It may worsen their observed all-time absolute-VCE limit instead of repairing the complete matrix. Exact sign, timestamp, emitter motion and bias response must be read from saved rows; unrelated extrema cannot establish the response.",
    "Hot-failing71/72 and87/88 are exact native cross-coupled C/B pairs in two parent instances130_1 and130_2, distinct from affectedC/D parents129_3 and129_4. The four C/D input shunts are not a demonstrated repair for these extra failures. Schematic aliases and simultaneous clock/data state remain to be joined."
  ],
  "new_native_simulation": false,
  "next_readback_requirements": [
    "Consume only already saved complete cloud captures for nominal/hot/cold cases. Authenticate native-result, parts and archive/member SHA identities before cloud-only acquisition. No new transient simulation is needed for diagnosis.",
    "At every original active minimum-VCE row and all-time maximum-abs-VCE row for all12failedIDs, retain simultaneous C/B/E terminal voltages, saved collector current, gain LP/LN, upper-master data-pair bases/emitters, selector base/collector/emitter, tail-MOS drain/source/gate, exact timestamp and original active-mask state.",
    "Retain clock cp/cn and data, sampler and comparator differential signals at those same rows; retain adjacent rows and fixed UI-relative event windows without choosing only favorable points. Verify row/time/column count, complete capture digest, and unchanged original screen replay.",
    "Measure same-row voltage differences across separately saved distributed RC terminal anchors. Do not treat a shared native topology net as an ideal equipotential when wire RC nodes are distinct.",
    "Preserve37.5ps sampler,75ps comparator,100mV signed margin,0.4V minimum active VCE,1.6V all-time absVCE and all original bias/phase/current gates. Compare any future physically changed candidate against all six PVT cases and four original controls."
  ],
